(text "DFFP_J2N16: pulse-clocked D flip-flop (one half of DFFP2_J2N16; its D inverter is on the parent sheet).\nBonch-Bruevich bistable (6N16B, cross-coupled through 470k || 3.9 pF / 200k) steered by two 6Zh2B: QN pentode g1 = S,\nQ pentode g1 = R, both g3 on G. Plates Ra 10k + La 1 mH (peaking: halves the flip time), screens Rg2 12k.\nC is the HV clock line: Cc 3.9 pF into G, which rests at -12.4 V (43k to GND, 130k to -50 V). The rising edge lifts G into\nthe g3 grid-current clamp for ~400 ns (above -5 V); the pentode whose g1 is high pulls its plate, the bistable finishes by regeneration.\nD and DN are HV: 150k / 62k dividers WITHOUT C1 into S and R. The g1 node (~5 pF) delays the data by ~150 ns, so a new D\nfrom the next flip-flop cannot reach the gate while the pulse lasts (the race margin). Each D pin loads its net by ~1.2 mA DC.\nSimulated, fanout 2/6: C -> Q 51-95 / 122-158 ns; setup 341/527 ns, hold -150/-3 ns; lowest grid -40 V (G, falling clock edge).\nHeater 6.3 V: 2 x 0.2 A + 0.4 A. Page: sch/logic/DFFP2_J2N16/README.md" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 213.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b0eef08e-b377-45bb-a6dc-e5918a0fa07d"))

